  "goodToKnow": "Hierzulande means in this country or here: Hierzulande ist Sonntag ein Ruhetag. It's very common in German journalism, avoiding the repetition of in Deutschland. Literally, it's hier zu Lande (here in the land), an old dative. The everyday equivalent is bei uns. The opposite idea, abroad, is im Ausland or, for the other side of an ocean, drüben."
